republic-function.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P5 (S16): "live well" is taken as faring well, being blessed and happy in P5 and as performing the soul's function (living) excellently where just_lives_well is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C2 (S18) does not follow (republic-function.logic.r3.sense1)
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C2 (S18): just_happy = F, just_lives_well = T, just_lives_well_2 = F, unjust_lives_ill = T, unjust_miserable = T
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P5 (S16): "lives ill" is taken as faring badly, being wretched in P5 and as performing the soul's function (living) badly where unjust_lives_ill is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C2 (S18) does not follow (republic-function.logic.r3.sense2)
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C2 (S18): just_happy = T, just_lives_well = T, unjust_lives_ill = T, unjust_lives_ill_2 = F, unjust_miserable = F
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P5 (S16): it takes "live well" from performing the soul's function (living) excellently to faring well, being blessed and happy, a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C2 (S18) does not follow (republic-function.logic.r3.sense3)
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C2 (S18): just_happy = F, just_lives_well = T, unjust_lives_ill = T, unjust_miserable = F
